-- title:
--   Inertia as the fixing subgroup of ℚₚ(μ_{p'})
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a natural number equipped with an instance asserting that it is prime, and let $\mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\ p$ be the chosen algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_p$. Consider the subset $S = \{\zeta : \exists N \in \mathbb{N},\ p \nmid N \text{ and } \zeta^N = 1\}$ of $\mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\ p$, that is, the set of roots of unity whose order is prime to $p$ (the condition $p \nmid N$ forces $N \neq 0$), and let $F_0 = \mathbb{Q}_p(S)$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\ p / \mathbb{Q}_p$ generated by $S$. The theorem asserts an equality of subgroups of the group $\mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\ p \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[\mathbb{Q}_p]} \mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\ p$ of $\mathbb{Q}_p$-algebra automorphisms: the fixing subgroup of $F_0$, i.e. the automorphisms fixing $F_0$ pointwise, coincides with `inertiaSubgroupIn` of the valuation subring $A$ of the canonical $\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$-valued valuation on $\mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\ p$ over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, namely the image, under the inclusion of the decomposition subgroup of $A$ into the full automorphism group, of those automorphisms that stabilise $A$ and act trivially on the residue field of $A$.
--
--   This identifies the fixed field of the inertia subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p/\mathbb{Q}_p)$ as the field generated by the roots of unity of order prime to $p$, i.e. as the maximal unramified extension $\mathbb{Q}_p^{\mathrm{nr}}$, in the form of an equality of a fixing subgroup with an inertia subgroup. It serves as the basic input for the local analysis of inertia in the completion bridge, and is used for criteria recognising membership in the inertia subgroup and for producing inertial elements moving a chosen element.
-- source:
